<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	App Sandbox is deliberately OFF. It only matters for Mac App Store
	submission, which this project doesn't target (see scripts/build_dmg.sh
	and README.md "Distributing a .dmg") — distribution here is a plain,
	ad-hoc-or-Developer-ID-signed .dmg, same as most non-Store Mac apps.
	Leaving it off also sidesteps real uncertainty this repo can't verify
	without a Mac: the app launches its bundled pdf_backend_cli helper
	(Process/NSTask) for every processing command, and that helper is a
	large PyInstaller-frozen binary doing its own file I/O — sandboxing
	that pairing has not been exercised on a real machine. If this app is
	ever submitted to the Mac App Store, re-enabling
	com.apple.security.app-sandbox and re-verifying the bundled-helper
	launch under sandbox constraints (or moving the backend into an XPC
	service) is a prerequisite, not an afterthought.

	No entitlement keys are set below: the com.apple.security.files.*
	grants only mean anything under App Sandbox, and without it the app has
	normal, unrestricted filesystem access (same as any other
	non-sandboxed Mac app) subject to the user's own macOS permissions.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
